From 69acded5552142f9cc402e2edfafb7a72e47d00b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:15:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] [Subtitles] Add keymap actions for the bitmap subtitle
 settings

The two settings added by the previous commit are reachable from the settings
screen and, like any setting, over JSON-RPC:

  {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"Settings.SetSettingValue",
   "params":{"setting":"subtitles.bitmapzoom","value":50}}

Neither of those is a button on a remote. Vertical position already has
subtitleshiftup/subtitleshiftdown for exactly that reason, so bitmap zoom gets
the same treatment:

  subtitlebitmapzoomin    enlarge by 5%
  subtitlebitmapzoomout   shrink by 5%
  subtitlebitmapposition  toggle whether the position and margin apply

The bounds come from the setting rather than being repeated in the handler, so
settings.xml stays the one place they are declared. The 5% increment is
deliberately not the setting's own step: that is 1%, chosen so the slider can be
adjusted finely, and a button that changes the size by 1% a press reads as doing
nothing at all.

The value is written through the settings manager, which means the renderer
picks it up mid-playback through the same OnSettingChanged path a GUI or
JSON-RPC change takes, with no special casing.

Deliberately not added to the add-on action id list in
kodi-dev-kit/include/kodi/c-api/gui/input/action_ids.h: keymaps and builtins do
not need it, and adding it there would make this an add-on API change, which
nothing here otherwise is.

Verified against a playing video: presses moved the setting in 5% steps in both
directions and the toggle flipped, with the value clamping at 10 and 200 rather
than overshooting or wrapping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
